# THE LAST LIGHT · Chapter 3 · The Storm
# Stage 3B: STAGE3_NARRATIVE_MASTER.md §8.3 and §11.1 (approved 2026-11-06).

== ch3_forecast mode=radio
! static
MORAG: All stations, all stations. This is Stornoway Coastguard. Gale warning.
MORAG: Hebrides, Minches. South-westerly severe gale nine, increasing storm ten, imminent.
MORAG: Visibility very poor. Stornoway out.
~ Ten. The windows are already shivering in their frames.

== ch3_corrie mode=radio
! static
CORRIE: North Point, Corrie May. Coming in from the east, and the sea's gone mad. I've lost the shore lights altogether. Over.
CALLUM: Corrie May, North Point. I'll put you in the East Gut. Confirm your position when I call. Over.

== ch3_lowestoft mode=radio
! static
LOWESTOFT: North Point Light, Lowestoft Star, Lowestoft Star. Coming down from the north with it on the bow.
LOWESTOFT: She won't hold her head up to it. Tell me where to steer, North Point. Over.
CALLUM: Lowestoft Star, North Point. Stand by. I've another boat on the East Gut. You're next. Over.
LOWESTOFT: Don't be long, North Point.

== ch3_after_two mode=thought
[if saved("Corrie May") and saved("Lowestoft Star")] ~ Both in. Both in. The engine's knocking like a fist on a table.
[if lost("Corrie May") or lost("Lowestoft Star")] ~ The radio fills up with Morag's voice and the lifeboat's, and then with nothing at all.
~ Coming up on two o'clock. I know what this hour sounds like in this room.

== ch3_elspeth mode=radio
! static
ELSPETH: North Point Light, this is motor vessel Iona Star, Iona Star. Passage report, over.
CALLUM: Iona Star, North Point. Go ahead, over.
ELSPETH: Glasgow for Stornoway, twelve souls aboard.
ELSPETH: We expect to pass abeam of your light at oh-five-hundred. Request local conditions, over.
CALLUM: Severe gale nine, storm ten imminent. Seas very high off the Gut. Keep well out to the east until you're past. Over.
ELSPETH: Understood. Keep well east. Who am I speaking to, North Point? Over.
* Callum Mackay, principal keeper. Over. -> name
* North Point Light. That's all you need. Over. -> curt
= name
ELSPETH(cold): Mackay.
! wait 1.2
ELSPETH(cold): My father's boat was lost under your light, Mr Mackay. Eighteen years ago tonight.
! set elspeth_named=1
ELSPETH: This is Elspeth Ross. First mate. I wanted you to know who was out here.
ELSPETH: Someone sent me a letter last month. No name on it. "The light was out. Your father was not to blame."
! set elspeth_letter_told=1
! wait 1.0
ELSPETH(cold): I'd like to know who writes a letter like that and doesn't sign it. Over.
* I'm sorry, Miss Ross. I was there that night. -> sorry_there
* I know who your father was. -> know
* (Say nothing.) -> silence
= sorry_there
! add rel.elspeth 1
! set told_elspeth_there=1
ELSPETH: ...Were you. Then you'll keep your light burning tonight. Iona Star out.
-> END
= know
ELSPETH(cold): Everyone knows who my father was. That was rather the point of the Inquiry. Iona Star out.
-> END
= silence
! add rel.elspeth -1
ELSPETH: ...Iona Star out.
-> END
= curt
! add rel.elspeth -1
ELSPETH: Thank you, North Point. That is all I need. Iona Star out.

== ch3_notes_a mode=radio
! static
MORAG: North Point, Stornoway. Callum, are you there? Over.
CALLUM(guarded): I'm here.
MORAG: I've something I should have said a long time ago.
MORAG: I've got it in front of me. My notebook from that night. Pencil. I kept it in my handbag for eighteen years like a fool.
MORAG: Mayday from Mary Ellen received at oh-one-fifty-two. And what he said was:
MORAG: "No light at North Point. Repeat. No light"

== ch3_dark mode=thought
! static fade
~ Bang. The room goes black.
~ Lamps out. Radio dead. Above my head the motor winds down and stops.
~ Only the red lamp on the distribution cabinet, glowing like a coal. The main breaker.

== ch3_notes_b mode=radio
! static
MORAG(worried): ...North Point! Callum! Answer me!
CALLUM: Lost the main breaker. I'm back. Light's back. Over.
MORAG(worried): Thank God. Callum, did you hear what I said?
MORAG: Oh-one-fifty-two. No light. Your father's log says the light failed at oh-two-ten. After she struck.
MORAG: Eighteen minutes, Callum. They hanged Alasdair Ross's name on eighteen minutes.
[if has_flag("admitted_once")] MORAG: And you told me tonight you'd missed lighting-up once. I've been sitting here working out which night.
[if has_flag("admitted_there")] MORAG: You told me you were there. So tell me.
[if has_flag("said_asleep")] MORAG: Asleep, you said. Then you'll not know what time it went out. Or will you.
* The log says oh-two-ten. The log is right. -> lie
* Morag, it was eighteen years ago. What does it matter now? -> deflect
* I was there. The light was out before she struck. -> admit
= lie
! set lied_to_morag=1
! add rel.morag -2
MORAG: ...Right.
MORAG: Right. I'll write that in my log, then. "North Point confirms the log." Stornoway out.
-> END
= deflect
! set deflected_morag=1
! add rel.morag -1
MORAG: It matters to six widows in Leverburgh, and to his. It matters to his girl. It matters to me, Callum. Stornoway out.
-> END
= admit
! set admitted_to_morag=1
! add rel.morag 2
MORAG: ...Oh, Callum.
MORAG: Not on the air. Not now. When this blows through, you and I are going to sit at my kitchen table. Stornoway listening.

== ch3_rory_dark mode=radio
! static
RORY: North Point, Kittiwake. Callum, you'll think I'm daft. Over.
CALLUM: Go ahead, Rory.
RORY: I'm tied up in the Sound, and I've been watching.
RORY: There's a boat came out from the lee of Pabbay. Old wooden boat, a wee motor-fisher. No lights. Not a single light, Callum.
RORY(scared): She's heading your way. Not for the Sound. For your landing, under the light. Over.
~ On the radar a small hard echo is moving in from the north, steady as a clock.

# ---- optional radio call (§11.1)

== opt_ch3_hector mode=radio
CALLUM: Gannet, North Point. Are you snug, Hector? Over.
! static
HECTOR: Snug as a dog in a basket, North Point. Two anchors down in the shelter of the West Gut.
HECTOR: And the passengers asleep at last. Over.
HECTOR: I was thinking of your father.
HECTOR: On a night like this he'd have had the kettle on and the tide tables open, and Sandy Ross up from the boat telling lies about herring.
* Sandy Ross? -> sandy
* He never spoke of it. -> never
= sandy
HECTOR: Alasdair. Nobody called him that but the minister. Sandy and Iain, thick as thieves, the summers Sandy ran the Board's stores.
HECTOR(sorry): Och. I'm sorry, Callum. I'm an old fool tonight. Gannet out.
! clue sandy
-> END
= never
HECTOR(sorry): No. He wouldn't, after. Nobody on Harris said the name for a long while. Gannet out.
! clue sandy

# ---- SCRIPT_REVISION_2026-11 (approved 2026-11-17): chapter 3 additions. The Hendrika spawns from the
# chapters.json beat hendrika_go (a ! ship line cannot carry JSON). ch3_fuel* are written for the Stage F
# fuel run and are not played until that beat exists.

== ch3_fuel mode=thought
~ Five past one. The day-tank glass is down on the red line.
~ She's run since four this afternoon. Down to the drums, then, and pump her up by hand.
~ The torch, and the stair door. Mind the ladder: it'll be wet in this.

== ch3_pump mode=thought
> [The hand pump: a dry rasp, then the suck and knock of diesel coming up]
~ Forty strokes and she's drawing. Twenty more.
~ That's near the bottom of the drum. I'll have stirred up every drop of water in it.

== ch3_fuel_done mode=thought
~ Day tank full. The door shut and dogged behind me.
~ A hundred and nine steps down to the base door, and nobody on them but me.

== ch3_sked_missed mode=radio
CALLUM: Sgeir Mhor, Sgeir Mhor, this is North Point. Two o'clock schedule. Over.
! wait 4
CALLUM: Sgeir Mhor, North Point. Murdo, do you hear me? Over.
! static
> [A carrier. No voice. Then nothing.]
~ Sgeir Mhor's off the air. Murdo will be at his batteries with a torch in his teeth.
~ If it can do that to Sgeir Mhor, it can do it here.

== ch3_hendrika mode=radio
! static
VISSER: North Point Light, North Point Light, this is Hendrika, Hendrika, Papa Echo Juliett X-ray. Over.
* Hendrika, North Point. Go ahead. Over. -> go
* Hendrika, North Point. Say your position. Over. -> pos
= go
VISSER: Good morning, North Point Light. I did not expect a voice at this hour. On my chart you are a light and nothing more. Over.
-> ask
= pos
VISSER: Five miles west of you, North Point Light, and not liking it. Over.
= ask
VISSER: I am timber for Stornoway, and late. My chart is the old edition.
VISSER: I would like the West Gut, please, if you will tell me it is still where my chart says. Over.
* She's where your chart says. Steer for the light, and I'll put you on the line. Over. -> help
* Stay outside, Hendrika. Heave to till morning. Over. -> outside
= help
! set helped_hendrika=1
VISSER: Thank you, North Point Light. My wife says you have a kind voice for such a bad night. Over.
-> END
= outside
VISSER: Understood. We will heave to and drink coffee. Hendrika out.

== ch3_hendrika_in mode=radio
[if saved("Hendrika")] VISSER: North Point Light, Hendrika. Anchored in the West Gut lee. Thank you. Over.
[if saved("Hendrika") and saved("Gannet")] VISSER: There is a schooner here also. Her master is waving a lamp at us. Over.
[if saved("Hendrika")] VISSER: My wife says to tell you, North Point. A good keeper. Hendrika out.
[if saved("Hendrika")] ~ A good keeper. He's no way of knowing any different.
[if lost("Hendrika")] ~ The Hendrika's echo goes into the broken water at the edge of the Gut, and doesn't come out.
[if lost("Hendrika")] ~ Morag's voice, calling the lifeboat. Then the lifeboat's, answering.
